      "side": 1,
      "message": "The first set of conditions tries to bypass groups with both dst and src cpus (same cluster migration, and current sched group is that cluster), so how about laying it out like this:\n\nif (cpumask_test_cpu(eenv-\u003esrc_cpu, sched_group_cpus(sg)) \u0026\u0026\n    cpumask_test_cpu(eenv-\u003edst_cpu, sched_group_cpus(sg)))) {\n        /* both cpus under consideration\n         * are in the same group, migration\n         * will not change group idle state\n         */\n        goto end;\n}\n\nif (cpumask_test_cpu(eenv-\u003esrc_cpu, sched_group_cpus(sg))) {\n        grp_util -\u003d eenv-\u003eutil_delta;\n} else if (cpumask_test_cpu(eenv-\u003edst_cpu, sched_group_cpus(sg))) {\n        grp_util +\u003d eenv-\u003eutil_delta;\n} else {\n        goto end;\n}\n\nWith appropriate comments where needed. I think this makes the code easier to read.",
